        min_points=2,
        model_answer="As the skydiver speeds up, air resistance increases, so the resultant force (weight minus air resistance) and hence the acceleration decrease. The gradient of the graph therefore gets smaller, producing a curve. When air resistance equals the weight the resultant force is zero, the acceleration is zero and the speed stays constant at the terminal velocity, so the line becomes horizontal.",
